                <pb facs="0464" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3442: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Des Fortes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-18T11:00:00-04:00">December 18, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. I am reliably informed that three of the League Commission members leave
                    today returning to Asunción after having received <pb facs="0465" n="377"
                        xml:id="pg377"/> agreement from Bolivia to integral arbitration. They expect
                    acceptance from President of Paraguay but difficulties with other leaders.</p>
                <p>Above sent to Montevideo, Asunción.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Des Portes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
